  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Dog Statue"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Dog Statue"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Statue of a Dog"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Statue of a Dog"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. The city-states, towns and villages of Shem are full of the dog as an esteemed part of everyday life. Often seen in various roles working as protectors and hearders in agricultural capacities as well as family pets. It is said that even some of the gods are accompanied by them as regular companions."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. The city-states, towns and villages of Shem are full of the dog as an esteemed part of everyday life. Often seen in various roles working as protectors and hearders in agricultural capacities as well as family pets. It is said that even some of the gods are accompanied by them as regular companions."
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian City-State Banner"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian City-State Banner"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian City-State Banner"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian City-State Banner"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Woven from fine silken fibers, this banner is decorated with intricate patterns that are seen in the central Iruk City-State district as an ornamental symbol of the region."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Woven from fine silken fibers, this banner is decorated with intricate patterns that are seen in the central Iruk City-State district as an ornamental symbol of the region."
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Well"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Well"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A water well similar to those seen in the City-State of Iruk"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A water well similar to those seen in the City-State of Iruk"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Throughout the lands of Shem, water is considered a precious resource and an essential element for survival. Any permanent settlement near water will inevitably be contested by others who also seek access to this life affirming resource.The convenience of a well allows building in areas that would otherwise be unsustainable. Wells fill with water over time and can be used to quench thirst, replenish waterskins and perform the dozens of other activities that require the presence of water."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Throughout the lands of Shem, water is considered a precious resource and an essential element for survival. Any permanent settlement near water will inevitably be contested by others who also seek access to this life affirming resource.The convenience of a well allows building in areas that would otherwise be unsustainable. Wells fill with water over time and can be used to quench thirst, replenish waterskins and perform the dozens of other activities that require the presence of water."
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Foundation"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Foundation"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A square foundation made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A square foundation made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It is said that a building is only as good as its foundation. Foundations provide the essential stability to anything built atop them and prevent the growth of plants beneath them.Placing a foundation is a significant act in the Exiled Lands. Once a foundation is placed by a clan or individual, that land is considered their territory. Nobody else can build in the immediate area unless the foundation is destroyed.Cut stone masonry is a time-tested building material that is traced back generations – even to the time of Atlantis. It provides a sense of permanence and scale fortifying a base against all but the strongest of siege weapons or cunning invaders. The specific architectural style emulates the light-colored masonry found in the great Shemite City-State of Iruk."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "It is said that a building is only as good as its foundation. Foundations provide the essential stability to anything built atop them and prevent the growth of plants beneath them.Placing a foundation is a significant act in the Exiled Lands. Once a foundation is placed by a clan or individual, that land is considered their territory. Nobody else can build in the immediate area unless the foundation is destroyed.Cut stone masonry is a time-tested building material that is traced back generations – even to the time of Atlantis. It provides a sense of permanence and scale fortifying a base against all but the strongest of siege weapons or cunning invaders. The specific architectural style emulates the light-colored masonry found in the great Shemite City-State of Iruk."
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Solid Wall"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Solid Wall"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A solid wall made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A solid wall made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Window Wall"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Window Wall"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A solid window wall made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A solid window wall made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Doorway"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Doorway"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A solid doorway made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A solid doorway made of cut stone blocks"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Stairs"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Stairs"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Stairs made of cut stone"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Stairs made of cut stone"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Any warrior with even a little battle hardening will agree that the safest ground to defend is the high ground. And if there is no high ground to defend, make it yourself.\nStairs are a necessity once buildings grow beyond a certain size. They provide points of natural defence and easy access to higher floors and rooftops (which make excellent archery platforms). Their only weakness is the material upon which they are built - if the high ground is brought crashing down then it no longer serves a tactical purpose.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Any warrior with even a little battle hardening will agree that the safest ground to defend is the high ground. And if there is no high ground to defend, make it yourself.\nStairs are a necessity once buildings grow beyond a certain size. They provide points of natural defence and easy access to higher floors and rooftops (which make excellent archery platforms). Their only weakness is the material upon which they are built - if the high ground is brought crashing down then it no longer serves a tactical purpose.\nReinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Door"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Door"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A heavy reinforced door"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A heavy reinforced door"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "One of the strongest doors that can be crafted, the heavy door offers protection against everything but the most powerful of enemy tricks.\nRaging hordes have been kept at bay by such doors and with a simple locking mechanism they become proof against incursions into structures.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "One of the strongest doors that can be crafted, the heavy door offers protection against everything but the most powerful of enemy tricks.\nRaging hordes have been kept at bay by such doors and with a simple locking mechanism they become proof against incursions into structures.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Sloped Roof"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Sloped Roof"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A sloped roof in the Irukian City-State style"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A sloped roof in the Irukian City-State style"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sloped roofs are practical in any weather as water and loose debris are simply repelled running off of the roof rather than accumulating inside buildings. Built of close tight fitting metal and cut stone, this will provide a safe haven and strong front to any foes who come knocking."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Sloped roofs are practical in any weather as water and loose debris are simply repelled running off of the roof rather than accumulating inside buildings. Built of close tight fitting metal and cut stone, this will provide a safe haven and strong front to any foes who come knocking."
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Irukian Ceiling"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Irukian Ceiling"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A ceiling made of metal and cut stone"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A ceiling made of metal and cut stone"
   },
   "Key": "Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
   },
