  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Consecrated Axes"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Consecrated Axes"
   },
   "Key": "1CFCC15646C591C4A7EB6FA077A13647"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Aesirian Greaves"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Aesirian Greaves"
   },
   "Key": "8A05CD364DE823AEFD432CAA32DED357"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Armored boots crafted in ancient Aesrian style"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Armored boots crafted in ancient Aesrian style"
   },
   "Key": "B5663D154BF8A59A31704498C623DA8A"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> “Swear not so often by Ymir,” uneasily muttered a warrior, glancing at the distant mountains. “This is his land and the god bides among yonder mountains, the legends say.”</> - The Frost-Giant’s Daughter By Robert E. Howard. These boots are comprised of both leather and steel plating to provide the wearer with both mobility and protection while at the same time keeping the feet warm."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> “Swear not so often by Ymir,” uneasily muttered a warrior, glancing at the distant mountains. “This is his land and the god bides among yonder mountains, the legends say.”</> - The Frost-Giant’s Daughter By Robert E. Howard. These boots are comprised of both leather and steel plating to provide the wearer with both mobility and protection while at the same time keeping the feet warm."
   },
   "Key": "E31486F446FE94C60AA381B671D1AD1F"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ice Wolf"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ice Wolf"
   },
   "Key": "C2E7F3FA492C4DC30FADE296885EC3D2"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Aesir have long held that wolves have a powerful place in folklore and legends. They often see wolves symbolizing strength, chaos and sometimes destiny. Aesir tribe legends speak of a pair of great ice wolves seen by Ymir's side symbolizing loyalty and wisdom. These two wolves embody fierce guardianship and the warrior's spirit typically accompanying Ymir in battle and in feasts. The Aesir believe that they personify the balance between savage nature and divine strategy, signaling the need to honor both primal instinctual drive and thoughtful actions in life. To honor Ymir, the Aesir have often taken in abandoned wolf pups to raise them as faithful companions and ferocious tribe protectors."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "The Aesir have long held that wolves have a powerful place in folklore and legends. They often see wolves symbolizing strength, chaos and sometimes destiny. Aesir tribe legends speak of a pair of great ice wolves seen by Ymir's side symbolizing loyalty and wisdom. These two wolves embody fierce guardianship and the warrior's spirit typically accompanying Ymir in battle and in feasts. The Aesir believe that they personify the balance between savage nature and divine strategy, signaling the need to honor both primal instinctual drive and thoughtful actions in life. To honor Ymir, the Aesir have often taken in abandoned wolf pups to raise them as faithful companions and ferocious tribe protectors."
   },
   "Key": "8386B499459CEBA5DBF88E9D268F94D6"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite Dungeon"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite Dungeon"
   },
   "Key": "ECB2F9FA4FD986923B7DAAAFB0F73AF7"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite Dungeon"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite Dungeon"
   },
   "Key": "B9AAD31648A0E70F56C5CD95985D4353"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Explorer's Journal"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Explorer's Journal"
   },
   "Key": "82D23D6F4BE77CB97D705F85ED31A3EA"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "We slipped in here under the cover of darkness to avoid the zealots out front. Rumors are that they capture animals and people only to use them as sacrifices to their god. We came in here for warmth and shelter during the night, but what is this place? It appears to be sealed up for some reason. We've heard tales from the elders of New Asagard that there is a shortcut through the mountain in this area - could this be it?"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "We slipped in here under the cover of darkness to avoid the zealots out front. Rumors are that they capture animals and people only to use them as sacrifices to their god. We came in here for warmth and shelter during the night, but what is this place? It appears to be sealed up for some reason. We've heard tales from the elders of New Asagard that there is a shortcut through the mountain in this area - could this be it?"
   },
   "Key": "B31E63234CFF643B21B331BF844AAD89"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zealot's Prayer to Ymir"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Zealot's Prayer to Ymir"
   },
   "Key": "340C7F27462015A04DC9E8AAD817B201"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "We commit these sacrifices to the void below in your name oh Great Ymir. Lord give us and our kin a bountiful harvest and mild seasons. Grant us the courage to fend off the giant kings and their allies. May our community be fruitful and our children healthy. Please accept this small sacrifice so it may please you. We ask this of you oh Great Ymir..."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "We commit these sacrifices to the void below in your name oh Great Ymir. Lord give us and our kin a bountiful harvest and mild seasons. Grant us the courage to fend off the giant kings and their allies. May our community be fruitful and our children healthy. Please accept this small sacrifice so it may please you. We ask this of you oh Great Ymir..."
   },
   "Key": "70A038444B545F2E0255C4B64CDA2853"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Wow, is this place dangerous! We broke through the ice barriers only to be chased by some unholy giants. All three of us jumped off into the pit below instead of fending them off. Thank god there was water at the bottom. This cavern is truly an amazing site to behold. The bridge above looks to be entirely made of some kind of ice. Although, we only managed to get halfway across until some insane wolf attacked us. We lept down once more to this ledge. There are only two of us now as the wolf is eating our comrade alive on the bridge above us. He is screaming while we huddle and listen to his flesh being ripped off and the crunch of ligaments and bones breaking. This is unbearable! We are not sure whether to climb back up to the bridge or try and find the ground below and get across that way. Maybe the wolf is full? We keep hearing strange sounds below... !"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Wow, is this place dangerous! We broke through the ice barriers only to be chased by some unholy giants. All three of us jumped off into the pit below instead of fending them off. Thank god there was water at the bottom. This cavern is truly an amazing site to behold. The bridge above looks to be entirely made of some kind of ice. Although, we only managed to get halfway across until some insane wolf attacked us. We lept down once more to this ledge. There are only two of us now as the wolf is eating our comrade alive on the bridge above us. He is screaming while we huddle and listen to his flesh being ripped off and the crunch of ligaments and bones breaking. This is unbearable! We are not sure whether to climb back up to the bridge or try and find the ground below and get across that way. Maybe the wolf is full? We keep hearing strange sounds below... !"
   },
   "Key": "ABFB5174490DADFF0A8F8DB9C755C762"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Explorer's Journal"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Explorer's Journal"
   },
   "Key": "892E3148474D605FB4FA94830EBBBE71"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Damn it! Another dive into the unknown! What kind of hell hole is this place!? The two of us managed to fend off these creepy ice goblins, but now what? Are we supposed to make another leap of faith? Maybe we can manage to climb down? I think we might be better off turning back."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Damn it! Another dive into the unknown! What kind of hell hole is this place!? The two of us managed to fend off these creepy ice goblins, but now what? Are we supposed to make another leap of faith? Maybe we can manage to climb down? I think we might be better off turning back."
   },
   "Key": "5126BEC44FB3841D967894A394051F07"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "My companion lept first and she missed the water below. She is lying dead on the rocks nearby. I am now the last of my party who came into the god forsaken cave. I hear whisperings of demons and those damn ice goblins nearby. I just want to get out of this place! I saw some ledges nearby and I will try to climb up to get a better look. Maybe I can see a way out?"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "My companion lept first and she missed the water below. She is lying dead on the rocks nearby. I am now the last of my party who came into the god forsaken cave. I hear whisperings of demons and those damn ice goblins nearby. I just want to get out of this place! I saw some ledges nearby and I will try to climb up to get a better look. Maybe I can see a way out?"
   },
   "Key": "D683627F46758499AD46688A536AF99B"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "What is this place? It looks like some kind of old ice cave, but why have the steps been carved up to the entryway. Who built this? Could this be the old shortcut through the mountain the Cimmerians told me about? It is far too cold out here so I will venture in to find temporary shelter and move on."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "What is this place? It looks like some kind of old ice cave, but why have the steps been carved up to the entryway. Who built this? Could this be the old shortcut through the mountain the Cimmerians told me about? It is far too cold out here so I will venture in to find temporary shelter and move on."
   },
   "Key": "318366F14CD6026591260494D7619830"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Pilgrim's Journal"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Pilgrim's Journal"
   },
   "Key": "BA8A896C451C2DB6014360991C0E40B7"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "We found this area of refuge last night to escape the blizzard. Thank Ymir we found it! I'm not sure what this place is. We heard rumors of a passage through the mountain, but we didn't have any luck finding it. It must be well hidden. There is something above us - growling, laughing - I'm not sure what. There is some kind of portal door here, but we dare not go in. The Zealots patrol this area and are ever present. We'll stay here overnight and continue our frost temple pilgrimage at first light."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "We found this area of refuge last night to escape the blizzard. Thank Ymir we found it! I'm not sure what this place is. We heard rumors of a passage through the mountain, but we didn't have any luck finding it. It must be well hidden. There is something above us - growling, laughing - I'm not sure what. There is some kind of portal door here, but we dare not go in. The Zealots patrol this area and are ever present. We'll stay here overnight and continue our frost temple pilgrimage at first light."
   },
   "Key": "7DE2DA484B1E5DD5031DCD95B2D1A4DB"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Lover's Lament"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Lover's Lament"
   },
   "Key": "9EB063F542E6E87C6184CF98EFF15CC4"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Here lies Ilga. She was a passionate and warm comfort in this frozen forest. I tried to save her, but alas she was taken and devoured in the middle of the night. I found her by this strange cave next to my dead horse with the flesh peeled clean from their bones and sheathed in ice. I can only imagine it must be what IIga called the Yakhmar. I remember tribal tales of a creature named Remora which did similar things to its victims. I feel responsible for her death and shall avenge her by slaying the creature. -Conan"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Here lies Ilga. She was a passionate and warm comfort in this frozen forest. I tried to save her, but alas she was taken and devoured in the middle of the night. I found her by this strange cave next to my dead horse with the flesh peeled clean from their bones and sheathed in ice. I can only imagine it must be what IIga called the Yakhmar. I remember tribal tales of a creature named Remora which did similar things to its victims. I feel responsible for her death and shall avenge her by slaying the creature. -Conan"
   },
   "Key": "8231A0B64440BEEDCB11F2B1CDD08A89"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Thank Ymir I found this area to escape the Ice Wurm below! I didn’t realize it would be here just lurking around. I think it might have offspring around here somewhere. I’ll stay here for a while until it is distracted and then I’ll make my escape. In the meantime, I found this strange mineral here called Tungsten, and I’m not sure what it is, or what it is used for. It looks more like brittle crystal than metal. I’ll harvest it and bring it back to the Cimmerian metallurgist in the village – maybe she can tell me more?"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Thank Ymir I found this area to escape the Ice Wurm below! I didn’t realize it would be here just lurking around. I think it might have offspring around here somewhere. I’ll stay here for a while until it is distracted and then I’ll make my escape. In the meantime, I found this strange mineral here called Tungsten, and I’m not sure what it is, or what it is used for. It looks more like brittle crystal than metal. I’ll harvest it and bring it back to the Cimmerian metallurgist in the village – maybe she can tell me more?"
   },
   "Key": "2421C0654D172DFB352942BF148FA6D2"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "I’m not too sure about this sorcery I’ve heard rumors of. The mounds of the dead area I traveled from seem to be ripe with sorcery of the undead – especially those glowing skeletons! I’ve been traveling to the legendary frost temple in the north to search for magic of the Aesir supposedly passed on by the mighty frost giant god Ymir. I ran into an old Cimmerian bear shaman that told me a story of a legendary Aesir sorcerer who could summon magical beasts with specialized ingredients. He said that he remembers this sorcerer talking about combining the carcass of a sabretooth, argossean dream dust as a catalyst, some kind of special alloy – tungsten he thought, and the heart of the demon wurm herself – Remora, to summon an ancient companion of Ymir. Although, he admitted he did not know in what quantity the ingredients needed to be in to work properly. He went on to caution me that none of these items were easy to come by and many a young sorcerer and shaman has ventured out in search of them only to never return. He did say that if someone was successful enough to find all the ingredients and then managed to summon one of these beasts that it would be a great and loyal warrior. Of course, he charged me gold for this story, and I think he was just swindling money out of me. Although, I’m sure sorcery of the Aesir and their god Ymir are somewhere around here to be found. These ice caves seem to go on in all kinds of directions so for the meantime I will keep searching this area before going onto the frost temple."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "I’m not too sure about this sorcery I’ve heard rumors of. The mounds of the dead area I traveled from seem to be ripe with sorcery of the undead – especially those glowing skeletons! I’ve been traveling to the legendary frost temple in the north to search for magic of the Aesir supposedly passed on by the mighty frost giant god Ymir. I ran into an old Cimmerian bear shaman that told me a story of a legendary Aesir sorcerer who could summon magical beasts with specialized ingredients. He said that he remembers this sorcerer talking about combining the carcass of a sabretooth, argossean dream dust as a catalyst, some kind of special alloy – tungsten he thought, and the heart of the demon wurm herself – Remora, to summon an ancient companion of Ymir. Although, he admitted he did not know in what quantity the ingredients needed to be in to work properly. He went on to caution me that none of these items were easy to come by and many a young sorcerer and shaman has ventured out in search of them only to never return. He did say that if someone was successful enough to find all the ingredients and then managed to summon one of these beasts that it would be a great and loyal warrior. Of course, he charged me gold for this story, and I think he was just swindling money out of me. Although, I’m sure sorcery of the Aesir and their god Ymir are somewhere around here to be found. These ice caves seem to go on in all kinds of directions so for the meantime I will keep searching this area before going onto the frost temple."
   },
   "Key": "497FEF6649B3470B638D4EA3E9A4F915"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Thank the gods we found this cave! Those beasts outside are terrible and very powerful. Especially, the polar bears. Although, it is to be suspected they would be this far north. I just didn’t think they’d be such voracious beasts. One chased our group and took one swat at our sherpa and broke him in half and then proceeded to eat his head. You know the old saying, how does one survive a bear attack, just be faster than your friend! In any case, I wonder if they can be tamed? Our Aesirian guide says there is a myth of old where Ymir rode on a mighty polar bear to keep watch over the northern tribes and any sighting of them by the clans would foreshadow an avalanche. He said that it was a story told by his grandsire to keep the clan’s children from wandering too far into the mountains. Though as a young man he remembered a Hyborian sorcerer coming to their village inquiring about the magic ingredients to summon a polar bear. Something about combining a dead polar bear cub, argossean dream dust, a large quantity of aesirian alloy, and the heart of Remora, to complete the spell.  It was a good story while we waited out the night in this freezing cave and helped pass the time, but I cannot help wondering if there is any truth to it. I could sure use a polar bear companion around here…"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Thank the gods we found this cave! Those beasts outside are terrible and very powerful. Especially, the polar bears. Although, it is to be suspected they would be this far north. I just didn’t think they’d be such voracious beasts. One chased our group and took one swat at our sherpa and broke him in half and then proceeded to eat his head. You know the old saying, how does one survive a bear attack, just be faster than your friend! In any case, I wonder if they can be tamed? Our Aesirian guide says there is a myth of old where Ymir rode on a mighty polar bear to keep watch over the northern tribes and any sighting of them by the clans would foreshadow an avalanche. He said that it was a story told by his grandsire to keep the clan’s children from wandering too far into the mountains. Though as a young man he remembered a Hyborian sorcerer coming to their village inquiring about the magic ingredients to summon a polar bear. Something about combining a dead polar bear cub, argossean dream dust, a large quantity of aesirian alloy, and the heart of Remora, to complete the spell.  It was a good story while we waited out the night in this freezing cave and helped pass the time, but I cannot help wondering if there is any truth to it. I could sure use a polar bear companion around here…"
   },
   "Key": "EE5CD82746F9E7F25BC77C824DE7763D"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite"
   },
   "Key": "0ED45B1A4D6311548869969C705F9C6A"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Respite"
   },
   "Translation": {
