  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Reforged Yoggite Cudgel"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Reforged Yoggite Cudgel"
   },
   "Key": "EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210277_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A macabre weapon of bone fused to rock."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A macabre weapon of bone fused to rock."
   },
   "Key": "EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210277_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Yog is lord of the empty places: the desert where voices die, the ruin where no hearth burns, the black gulf between the stars. His faithful carried weapons for their oldest commandment: eat no green thing, and let no meat go unclaimed.</>\n\nThis cudgel is a sacred weapon carried by the faithful of Yog.\n\n<LoreItalics>Gnawing Hunger: Your direct weapon attacks can trigger Gnawing Hunger, dealing up to 90 Entropic damage based on the target's remaining health. The effect is strongest against a fresh target and fades sharply as the target approaches death.</>\n\n<LoreItalics>Entropic magic damage sometimes amplifies all physical damage taken by the target for a short while.</>\n\n<LoreItalics>Adaptive weapons use your higher weapon damage attribute, Strength or Agility, and benefit from the matching bonus weapon damage stat on your armor.</>"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Yog is lord of the empty places: the desert where voices die, the ruin where no hearth burns, the black gulf between the stars. His faithful carried weapons for their oldest commandment: eat no green thing, and let no meat go unclaimed.</>\n\nThis cudgel is a sacred weapon carried by the faithful of Yog.\n\n<LoreItalics>Gnawing Hunger: Your direct weapon attacks can trigger Gnawing Hunger, dealing up to 90 Entropic damage based on the target's remaining health. The effect is strongest against a fresh target and fades sharply as the target approaches death.</>\n\n<LoreItalics>Entropic magic damage sometimes amplifies all physical damage taken by the target for a short while.</>\n\n<LoreItalics>Adaptive weapons use your higher weapon damage attribute, Strength or Agility, and benefit from the matching bonus weapon damage stat on your armor.</>"
   },
   "Key": "EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210277_LongDesc"
  },
