   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>A long bow and a strong bow, and let the sky grow dark! The cord to the nock, the shaft to the ear, and the king of Koth for a mark!</> - Song of the Bossonian Archers.\r\n\r\nCarved from a single piece of wood, the hunting bow is used across the world and in hundreds of variants.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle.\r\n\r\nThis bow will be able to bring down both human and non-human foes, but it relies heavily on the skill of the wielder."
   },
   "Key": "9146F25640FC26E80A3BBA9E15157C9D"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Springing to his feet, he bent his bow powerfully and drove his last shaft point blank at a great hairy shape that soared up at his throat. The arrow was a flying beam of moonlight that flashed onward with but a blur in its course, but the were-beast plunged convulsively in midair and crashed headlong, shot through and through.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nCreated based on an ancient design found in the Exiled Lands, this bow seems to confuse the eye with its odd, alien curves.\r\n\r\nIn the thrum of the bowstring, it whispers of gibbering terrors screeching beneath a blood-red moon and the terrified screams of those who flee the merciless hunt.\r\n\r\nOne who holds this bow too long risks being drawn into its miasma of madness."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Springing to his feet, he bent his bow powerfully and drove his last shaft point blank at a great hairy shape that soared up at his throat. The arrow was a flying beam of moonlight that flashed onward with but a blur in its course, but the were-beast plunged convulsively in midair and crashed headlong, shot through and through.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nCreated based on an ancient design found in the Exiled Lands, this bow seems to confuse the eye with its odd, alien curves.\r\n\r\nIn the thrum of the bowstring, it whispers of gibbering terrors screeching beneath a blood-red moon and the terrified screams of those who flee the merciless hunt.\r\n\r\nOne who holds this bow too long risks being drawn into its miasma of madness."
