  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Brutal Yoggite Watcher Mask"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Brutal Yoggite Watcher Mask"
   },
   "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952511_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A ritual mask used by Yoggite shamans to see the dead"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A ritual mask used by Yoggite shamans to see the dead"
   },
   "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952511_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Carved into solid wood and decorated with intricate symbols, the watcher mask is said to remove the veil between the wearer and the spiritual world where Yog dwells.\nDarfari slaves, captured and carried into the Hyborian kingdoms do not have shamans of their own, and are forced to practise a perverted version of their religion. They have long since lost the art of creating masks such as these.\nBut in the southern deserts, Darfari shamans practise a purer version of the religion. Through the aid of these masks they can see the dead and, it is rumored, manifestations of Yog himself.\n\nThis mask offers some protection from both weapons and the elements.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Carved into solid wood and decorated with intricate symbols, the watcher mask is said to remove the veil between the wearer and the spiritual world where Yog dwells.\nDarfari slaves, captured and carried into the Hyborian kingdoms do not have shamans of their own, and are forced to practise a perverted version of their religion. They have long since lost the art of creating masks such as these.\nBut in the southern deserts, Darfari shamans practise a purer version of the religion. Through the aid of these masks they can see the dead and, it is rumored, manifestations of Yog himself.\n\nThis mask offers some protection from both weapons and the elements.\n"
   },
   "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952511_LongDesc"
  },
