  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Slaver Waistguard"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Slaver Waistguard"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A waistguard designed to intimidate"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A waistguard designed to intimidate"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">There was a giant Hyperborean renegade, taciturn, dangerous, with a broadsword strapped to his gaunt frame -- for men wore steel openly in the Maul.</> - The Tower of the Elephant\n\nIn the far north, east of the lands of the Nordheimers, live the tall, gaunt people known as the Hyperboreans. Ruled by the White Hand, a cabal of sorcerers, they often stage raids into Cimmeria to take slaves for their sorcerous experiments.\n\nIt is considered a challenge among Hyperborean slavers to go bare-chested on their raids, wearing nothing more than this waistguard. While it offers less protection than steel leggings and a breastplate, it intimidates newly caught slaves into submission."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">There was a giant Hyperborean renegade, taciturn, dangerous, with a broadsword strapped to his gaunt frame -- for men wore steel openly in the Maul.</> - The Tower of the Elephant\n\nIn the far north, east of the lands of the Nordheimers, live the tall, gaunt people known as the Hyperboreans. Ruled by the White Hand, a cabal of sorcerers, they often stage raids into Cimmeria to take slaves for their sorcerous experiments.\n\nIt is considered a challenge among Hyperborean slavers to go bare-chested on their raids, wearing nothing more than this waistguard. While it offers less protection than steel leggings and a breastplate, it intimidates newly caught slaves into submission."
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Legendary"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Legendary"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Armor"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Armor"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_SecondModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "SlaverGuard"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "SlaverGuard"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483018_ThirdModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Slaver Loincloth"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Slaver Loincloth"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483019_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A loincloth worn beneath by Hyperborean slavers"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A loincloth worn beneath by Hyperborean slavers"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483019_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">There was a giant Hyperborean renegade, taciturn, dangerous, with a broadsword strapped to his gaunt frame -- for men wore steel openly in the Maul.</> - The Tower of the Elephant\n\nIn the far north, east of the lands of the Nordheimers, live the tall, gaunt people known as the Hyperboreans. Ruled by the White Hand, a cabal of sorcerers, they often stage raids into Cimmeria to take slaves for their sorcerous experiments.\n\nPrimarily worn beneath the more armored waistguard, this loincloth is designed to keep the vitals of a slaver warm and protected when on long raids in the northern lands of Asgard and Vanaheim."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">There was a giant Hyperborean renegade, taciturn, dangerous, with a broadsword strapped to his gaunt frame -- for men wore steel openly in the Maul.</> - The Tower of the Elephant\n\nIn the far north, east of the lands of the Nordheimers, live the tall, gaunt people known as the Hyperboreans. Ruled by the White Hand, a cabal of sorcerers, they often stage raids into Cimmeria to take slaves for their sorcerous experiments.\n\nPrimarily worn beneath the more armored waistguard, this loincloth is designed to keep the vitals of a slaver warm and protected when on long raids in the northern lands of Asgard and Vanaheim."
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483019_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Legendary"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Legendary"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483019_FirstModifier"
  },
