  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ornate gown designed for Lemurian royalty"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "An ornate gown designed for Lemurian royalty"
   },
   "Key": "dt_Ma_Table_147483027_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The rulers of ancient Lemuria were, without exception, women. They worshipped Dagon and any male heirs to the throne were given in sacrifice to the Demon of the Depths.\n\nThe royal garments are therefore designed to be worn by their Witch Queens. Which explains their femininity, if not exactly why some men insist on wearing them.\n\nIt is clear that the designers of the royal Lemurian clothing were also responsible for the design of the bracelet that imprisons people in the Exiled Lands. Another mystery."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "The rulers of ancient Lemuria were, without exception, women. They worshipped Dagon and any male heirs to the throne were given in sacrifice to the Demon of the Depths.\n\nThe royal garments are therefore designed to be worn by their Witch Queens. Which explains their femininity, if not exactly why some men insist on wearing them.\n\nIt is clear that the designers of the royal Lemurian clothing were also responsible for the design of the bracelet that imprisons people in the Exiled Lands. Another mystery."
