  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nAncient Civilization Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.\nA barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.\nJust remember to add a door.\nAncient Civilization Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790302_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Cold Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Cold Insulated"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790302_FirstModifier"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient Civ Tiled Sloped Roof"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ancient Civ Tiled Sloped Roof"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790274_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tiled sloped roof piece"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A tiled sloped roof piece"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790274_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sloped rooves are practical in sandstorms as the loose debris simply runs from the roof rather than accumulating.\nAncient Civilization Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Sloped rooves are practical in sandstorms as the loose debris simply runs from the roof rather than accumulating.\nAncient Civilization Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790274_LongDesc"
