  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient Civ Sloping Wall"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Ancient Civ Sloping Wall"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790311_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A sloping wallpiece"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A sloping wallpiece"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790311_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "These walls are useful for filling out gaps left by odd building pieces.\nBlack Ice-Reinforced Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n\n"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "These walls are useful for filling out gaps left by odd building pieces.\nBlack Ice-Reinforced Wood  is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.\n\n"
   },
   "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790311_LongDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Insulated"
