  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Yog Cleaver"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Blessed Yog Cleaver"
   },
   "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51458_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rudimentary axe created from a jawbone bound to a stout branch"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A rudimentary axe created from a jawbone bound to a stout branch"
   },
   "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51458_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> On the heels of the shout came a clamor of blood-freezing screams, the shattering impact of axes on the gate.</> - The Black Stranger\n\nBladed weapons are generally frowned upon by the worshippers of Yog, but this jawbone is dull enough that it acts more like a club than a sword.\nYoggites believe that the consumption of human flesh gives them the Blessing of Yog for a period of time, which grants them invulnerability to normal weapons.\n\nWhile Yog is considered a deity in Darfar, scholars in Hyboria classify him as a demon of the Elder night, referencing ancient documents that survived the drowning of Atlantis."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> On the heels of the shout came a clamor of blood-freezing screams, the shattering impact of axes on the gate.</> - The Black Stranger\n\nBladed weapons are generally frowned upon by the worshippers of Yog, but this jawbone is dull enough that it acts more like a club than a sword.\nYoggites believe that the consumption of human flesh gives them the Blessing of Yog for a period of time, which grants them invulnerability to normal weapons.\n\nWhile Yog is considered a deity in Darfar, scholars in Hyboria classify him as a demon of the Elder night, referencing ancient documents that survived the drowning of Atlantis."
   },
