  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zathite Ritual Dagger"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Zathite Ritual Dagger"
   },
   "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51908_Name"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A venom-tipped dagger used in Zathite rituals"
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "A venom-tipped dagger used in Zathite rituals"
   },
   "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51908_ShortDesc"
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zath is a god who speaks of purity to his cult, predicting that he will one day arise and sweep across the land, cleansing it of decadence. His cultists work to spread his work and works throughout the kingdom of Zamoria.\n\nCarried by Exiles to the Exiled Lands and the Isle of Siptah, the teachings of the god have found followers among those who feel abandoned by their regular gods.\n\nThe primary means of execution for those who disobey the commandments of Zath is to put them in the tunnels beneath the great temple in Yezud and allow the to be devoured by Zath and his children. This is a ritual of purification and the dead are considered blessed by Zath. Their corpses are burned in the eternal flame of the temple as an offering to Zath.\n\nFor those who are far from Yezud, this dagger tipped in venom will have to take the place of a venomous spider."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "Zath is a god who speaks of purity to his cult, predicting that he will one day arise and sweep across the land, cleansing it of decadence. His cultists work to spread his work and works throughout the kingdom of Zamoria.\n\nCarried by Exiles to the Exiled Lands and the Isle of Siptah, the teachings of the god have found followers among those who feel abandoned by their regular gods.\n\nThe primary means of execution for those who disobey the commandments of Zath is to put them in the tunnels beneath the great temple in Yezud and allow the to be devoured by Zath and his children. This is a ritual of purification and the dead are considered blessed by Zath. Their corpses are burned in the eternal flame of the temple as an offering to Zath.\n\nFor those who are far from Yezud, this dagger tipped in venom will have to take the place of a venomous spider."
   },
