  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "\"Legionaries of the late Republic and early Empire often carried two pila, with one sometimes being lighter than the other. Standard tactics called for Roman soldiers to throw one of them (both if time permitted) at the enemy, just before charging to engage with the gladius.\" Commissioned by JimothyJamothy."
   },
   "Translation": {
    "Text": "\"Legionaries of the late Republic and early Empire often carried two pila, with one sometimes being lighter than the other. Standard tactics called for Roman soldiers to throw one of them (both if time permitted) at the enemy, just before charging to engage with the gladius.\" Commissioned by JimothyJamothy."
   },
   "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2491790_LongDesc"
  },
